nce I don't have any other W tiles except W4, maybe it's not useful.\n\nSo maybe T3 is the better choice.\n\nAnother angle: the unshown tiles. T3 has 3 left, which is more than some others. So discarding T3 is safer.\n\nSo after evaluating, I think the best move is to discard T3. This removes a tile that's not part of any current meld and is less likely to be needed by others, given the other players' melds.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: The hand has a pair of T9 and potential pairs in J1/J2, but lacks sufficient melds. Discarding T3 is optimal as it's part of a completed meld by the player across, reducing risk of aiding others.  \nReason: T3 is part of the player across's T2-T3-T4 meld, making it safe to discard. This maintains potential pairs in J1/J2 and T9 while minimizing risk.  \nAnswer: Play T3"}
